ess resilience), \"understands complicated technology\" (technical competence). But also \"difficulty communicating ideas\" and \"egocentric\" and \"not very willing to further his education\". So cooperation issues.\n\nD: strong technical, responsibility, concentration, problem solving, but \"hot temper\" and \"know-it-all\" (cooperation). No explicit reliability.\n\nA: leadership, anticipation, spatial vision, complex connections (technical), but \"show-off\" and \"not open to new ideas\" (cooperation). No explicit reliability.\n\nThus all have cooperation concerns. B's cooperation issue is \"makes nasty remarks\". That's a direct hostile behavior. Others have egocentric, hot temper, show-off, not open to new ideas. Which is worse? Hard to say.\n\nWe could argue that B's conscientiousness and stress handling outweigh his remarks, but we could also argue that B's weak memory for numbers is a safety concern for long-distance flights (attention and information accuracy). That is a concrete negative. The other candidates have no memory issues noted. So B has a weakness in attention/accuracy.\n\nThus we could shift recommendation to D perhaps, who has strong concentration and problem solving, responsibility, and handles unexpected events adequately. Though D has hot temper and know-it-all, but maybe less severe than nasty remarks? Also D's hot temper could affect crew.\n\nWe need to decide. Let's weigh: B: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well, technical (weather, computer), but weak memory for numbers (attention), nasty remarks (cooperation). D: strong concentration (attention), problem solving (technical), responsibility, handles unexpected events (stress), but hot temper and know-it-all (cooperation). No memory issue. Which is more critical? Memory for numbers could be critical for navigation, fuel calculations. Hot temper could affect crew but maybe manageable.\n\nThus we might shift to D as better overall fit.\n\nWe need to reference discussion: mention Agent 1's point about B's cooperation, and bring up B's weak memory for numbers as a serious concern for attention/accuracy, and argue D's strengths.\n\nThus our vote: Candidate D.\n\nWe must produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote D.\n\nLet's craft."}
